First Author: Zhou
Title: Prediction of 1-year mortality after heart transplantation using machine learning approaches: A single-center study from China
Source number: 57  ￼

Very short summary: This single-center Chinese study developed machine-learning models to predict 1-year mortality after heart transplantation. Five key findings were: (1) 381 orthotopic heart-transplant recipients were included; (2) overall 1-year survival was 84.8%; (3) 13 candidate variables were selected and all retained after LASSO; (4) the random forest model had the best discrimination with AUC 0.801, while gradient boosting machine had the highest sensitivity at 0.271; and (5) albumin, recipient age, and left atrial diameter were the top three predictors, with SHAP used to explain individual predictions. Figures 1–5 and Tables 1–2 were directly used for this extraction.  ￼

