	•	Section 3 Comments/Quotes: Seven machine-learning approaches were trained after LASSO feature selection. The best-performing model was random forest. Inputs were structured recipient and donor variables from electronic medical records. The data were randomly split 70%/30% into training and testing sets, and parameters were tuned using grid search with five-fold cross-validation. SHAP was explicitly used for model interpretation.  ￼

