	•	Section 5 Comments/Quotes: The primary endpoint was “postoperative 1-year mortality,” which maps to 1-year survival in this extraction framework. Under bootstrap validation, the random forest model achieved the best AUC of 0.801, with accuracy 0.828, sensitivity 0.268, and specificity 0.927. GBM had slightly lower AUC 0.786 but the highest sensitivity 0.271. PPV/NPV were not reported numerically in the shown results tables, and calibration and DCA were not reported.  ￼

